Package: gaia
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/Warewave-Technology/gaia
Recommends: qemu-system-x86, qemu-utils, libvirt-daemon-system, libvirt-clients, dnsmasq-base, iproute2
Suggests: podman, uidmap, crun, catatonit, fuse-overlayfs, ovmf
Description: backup and recoverability server with proven restores
 Gaia backs up VMs on KVM hosts over SSH, restores them in an isolated sandbox
 on a schedule to prove they boot, and records every proof as signed evidence
 an auditor can verify offline. It also checks, read-only, whether VMware VMs
 would run on KVM.
 .
 The package installs the program (/usr/bin/gaia) and its three services:
 gaia (the server), gaia-sandbox (restore tests) and gaia-convert (migration
 checks). None is started until it is set up: see
 /usr/share/doc/gaia/install.md.
